  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 8",
  "description": "Release 8 of the HBN-EEG dataset, the EEG component of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network project, organized in BIDS format. It contains EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 257 children and young adults (ages 5-21) performing six passive and active tasks: resting state, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, and symbol search. Events carry Hierarchical Event Descriptor (HED) annotations, and the participants file includes CBCL-derived psychopathology factors and quality-control results.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded while participants completed six tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files with HED annotations. Minimal quality control checked for file corruption and the presence of required events for each task, with results stored in participants.tsv.",
